From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:38:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): make the phone Settings menu read as a list of
 pages

On phones the Settings drawer is the whole menu, but it looked exactly
like the sidebar: bare /settings highlighted General although no page
was open, rows had no disclosure cue, and rows stayed about 33px tall
while the primary navigation already has 44px touch targets.

In the phone drawer the settings nav now shows a chevron Back row, a large
Settings title, the search field under the title, sections as rounded
inset groups with hairline separators, and 44px rows with a trailing
chevron. Like a phone settings list, no row is highlighted (bare
/settings redirects to General, which used to look selected); the open
section keeps aria-current for assistive tech. While a search shows
results they take the place of the groups as before, under the title.
The desktop layout, and a window wide enough to dock the menu beside the
page, keep the sidebar rows and the highlight.
The menu counts as docked when the sidebar hands it onCollapse, which it
does only then. Importing the side-by-side hook instead would read the
breakpoint from the mobile hook's module, which many tests mock with the
hook alone.

Not upstream yet: proposed from feat/mobile-settings-nav; drop this copy once it merges.

Docs: none (layout polish of the phone Settings menu; nothing to configure)
